{"parentUuid":"9222da57-818c-48c2-8057-8cb65bf96f1a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac7100d52d01adab3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqKVnUEbRReAwwNSv7H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U5USBhgETDDvQ45DgUD78a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/; grep -n \"fairly random\" framework--descriptive*.md | cut -c1-600; grep -n \"modern conditions\" framework--seven*.md | cut -c1-700; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np={int(k):v for k,v in json.load(open('/tmp/r2/pages.json')).items()}\nfor k in (389,390):\n  t=' '.join(p[k].split())\n  i=t.find('modern')\n  while i!=-1: print(k,t[max(0,i-250):i+100]); i=t.find('modern',i+1)\nEOF","description":"Check two flagged quotes in GO entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_read_input_tokens":169585,"output_tokens":467,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2648},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":169585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2648,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U5USBhgETDDvQ45DgUD78a":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/; grep -n \"fairly random\" framework--descriptive*.md | cut -c1-600; grep -n \"modern conditions\" framework--seven*.md | cut -c1-700; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np={int(k):v for k,v in json.load(open('/tmp/r2/pages.json')).items()}\nfor k in (389,390):\n  t=' '.join(p[k].split())\n  i=t.find('modern')\n  while i!=-1: print(k,t[max(0,i-250):i+100]); i=t.find('modern',i+1)\nEOF","description":"Check two flagged quotes in GO entries"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffqKPsXRQ9kCYfBo3Pya","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"043bc273-8e0a-490b-9c83-1a817242b17b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:11:43.075Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"043bc273-8e0a-490b-9c83-1a817242b17b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ce914f6b-f81b-42fd-a40b-4c5550786125","agentId":"ac7100d52d01adab3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5USBhgETDDvQ45DgUD78a","type":"tool_result","content":"23:On measurement: \"It is of little value to identify which energy systems, types of fitness or movement patterns are involved in a sport unless accurate numerical determinations are regularly made of each of these factors. Even then, we have to remember that the body is not simply a machine in which input and output are deterministically related, but an organism whose behaviour displays non-linearity and fairly random deviations... Nevertheless, without this information, long-term programming becomes imprecise\" (PDF p. 391, checked against the page image). The descriptive-modelling passage na\n29:**When NOT to apply** — The authors themselves warn that the body is non-linear and deviates \"fairly random[ly]\" from quantitative prediction, so a model is a guide, not a forecast. Their example norms (Tables 6.6-6.12) come from Soviet track-and-field and weightlifting populations of the 1970s and 1980s and are \"not... all-embracing models\" (PDF p. 391; the sentence is printed with a double negative, \"None of these examples should not be regarded as all-embracing models\"). No football descriptive model is given.\n16:**What it is** — The authors condense 6.12 into seven aims that \"become the definitive rules of programming\" for \"highly qualified athletes under modern conditions\" (PDF p. 389 / printed p. 378, and PDF p. 390 / printed p. 379, both checked against the page images). Paraphrased with the key wording:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cbb9e237-b21c-4937-93a8-3fbe27206266","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:11:43.389Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"23:On measurement: \"It is of little value to identify which energy systems, types of fitness or movement patterns are involved in a sport unless accurate numerical determinations are regularly made of each of these factors. Even then, we have to remember that the body is not simply a machine in which input and output are deterministically related, but an organism whose behaviour displays non-linearity and fairly random deviations... Nevertheless, without this information, long-term programming becomes imprecise\" (PDF p. 391, checked against the page image). The descriptive-modelling passage na\n29:**When NOT to apply** — The authors themselves warn that the body is non-linear and deviates \"fairly random[ly]\" from quantitative prediction, so a model is a guide, not a forecast. Their example norms (Tables 6.6-6.12) come from Soviet track-and-field and weightlifting populations of the 1970s and 1980s and are \"not... all-embracing models\" (PDF p. 391; the sentence is printed with a double negative, \"None of these examples should not be regarded as all-embracing models\"). No football descriptive model is given.\n16:**What it is** — The authors condense 6.12 into seven aims that \"become the definitive rules of programming\" for \"highly qualified athletes under modern conditions\" (PDF p. 389 / printed p. 378, and PDF p. 390 / printed p. 379, both checked against the page images). Paraphrased with the key wording:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"043bc273-8e0a-490b-9c83-1a817242b17b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
