{"parentUuid":"fd1e6b95-83ec-455a-9f0b-0b14c3d1cead","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac7100d52d01adab3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffr5A8WuQxqS8cAm149d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** 22 entries are GO, 3 need a fix, and none is NO-GO. Of the 11 files round 1 marked FIX, 9 are now GO and 2 need one more pass. One round-1 GO entry (the endurance models) is now FIX. All three fixes are a sentence or a label:\n\n1. **`framework--annual-models-for-medium-and-long-duration-endurance-sports`:** change the confidence to `contested`, with the reason in the entry. It also still says the models carry \"the same Issurin 2016 challenge\" as the explosive-strength entry. That entry now says Issurin 2016 does not count against the model in its own domain, so the pointer contradicts its target. This mismatch came in during the fix round.\n2. **`claim--complex-training-falls-short-for-highly-qualified-athletes`:** it presents only Issurin 2016 as disputing the book's \"complex training is for beginners\" limit. Issurin's own 2008 book agrees with that limit: the traditional complex model \"has visible benefits for the preparation of low- and mid-level athletes\" (Block Periodization PDF p. 44 / printed p. 33). The vault already records this split. Add that line and say the contest rests on the 2016 review only.\n3. **`claim--two-large-mesocycles-a-year-bi-cyclic-organisation`:** the \"terminology tension\" paragraph is the writer's interpretation written as if the authors said it. It needs an \"Inference:\" label.\n\n**Explosive-strength entry: GO.**\n- I measured Fig 6.39 myself at 400 dpi against the month ticks. Every phase, block and curve statement holds, including blocks 1 and 2, the dip and rebound of the strength curves, and Technique and the GPP/Speed curves.\n- Every Issurin quote matches the brief or the Issurin entries word for word.\n- The brief does not say \"jumping-type sports.\" It uses \"jumping\" once, in its list of populations (p. 11), and describes where the concentrated model fits only as \"sports dominated by a narrow target quality.\" The fixer was right on this.\n- The football scoping is correct. Issurin's book is the in-domain basis for `contested`, and Issurin 2016 is applied only to transferring the model to football.\n- Two optional touches: the block-2 lows sit nearer month 7 than \"months 6-7\", and the comparison with Issurin's season structure could carry an \"Inference:\" label.\n\n**Endurance entry: it should be `contested`, on brief p. 6.**\n- **Swimming is inside the entry's own domain.** The book counts swimming among the cyclic sports where the delayed effect of concentrated strength blocks was observed (PDF 374), and scopes the medium-duration model to \"cyclic sports of medium duration\" (PDF 399).\n- **The brief names swimming directly.** Brief p. 6 gives an elite-swimmer example (performance improved in only two of three athletes). It also judges the evidence \"insufficient for broad implementation in high-performance combat, team-sport, and swimming preparation.\"\n- **The same rule already moved the tri-cyclic entry to `contested`.** The book also lists swimming as a sport that traditionally uses three-cycle years (PDF 387). That does not remove it from the endurance domain.\n\nWith this change the chapter has 6 `contested`, 18 `supported` and 1 `untested`.\n\n**Is the domain rule applied consistently?** Yes, for the explosive, tri-cyclic, two-mesocycles, complex-training and concentrated-loading entries. The only inconsistency is the endurance entry. All 7 of the fixer's disagreements with round 1 hold up. I re-read Figs 6.32(b) and 6.36(b) myself, and the fixer's readings of both are right.\n\n**GO entries I spot-checked against the pages:**\n- `claim--concentrated-strength-loading-limited-period-qualified-athletes-and-volume-saving`\n- `framework--mesocycle-variants-smooth-rise-versus-concentrated-dip-and-rebound` (including the Fig 6.33 image)\n- `heuristic--set-mesocycle-boundaries-by-main-competition-dates`\n- `framework--eight-step-sequence-for-programming-annual-training`\n\nI also read the two GO entries the fixer edited in full. The descriptive-models entry is right, with Tables 6.7-6.12 checked value by value. The endurance entry is the FIX above.\n\n**Checks on all 25 files:**\n- Every quote matched the source text. Nothing was misquoted.\n- All 25 pass the format checks: six section headers, no stray em dashes, no wrapped or broken links, no review-history wording.\n- The fix log's 18 old phrases are all gone, and its confidence count (19 `supported`, 5 `contested`, 1 `untested`) matches the files.\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6d_opus_round2.md`, and the page renders are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r2_6d_*.png`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":229939,"output_tokens":1712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1712,"cache_read_input_tokens":229939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":404,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":404,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cffr52Fk65RZWLs91SEFa","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ee83ea19-beef-4163-89e7-dfb21fca5210","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:21:45.733Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"